Package: selectiveHotelling
Title: Selective Hotelling T-squared Testing After k-Means Clustering with
    Unknown Covariance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Yiqun", "Chen", , "yiqun.t.chen@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Valid selective inference for a Hotelling T-squared test comparing
    the means of two clusters discovered by k-means clustering, treating the
    covariance matrix as unknown. Monte Carlo p-values are computed by sampling
    the polar factor uniformly within the data-driven selection region on the
    Stiefel manifold, extending the selective inference framework of Chen and
    Witten (2023) to the unknown-covariance setting.
